  "id": "COMPOUND:32301 - PROTEIN:5777",
  "verbalization": "Dodonolide is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SF-188 through a series of molecular interactions involving hepatocytes. The evidence suggests that Dodonolide targets hepatocytes, which in turn are targeted by multiple compounds, including (5R,7S,8S)-5-hydroxy-4-methoxy-7,8-dimethyl-7,8-dihydro-5H-pyrano[4,3-b]pyran-2-one and 5-Propyloxolan-2-One, all of which ultimately have SF-188 as their target. This indicates a potential shared mechanism of action or a common downstream effect in the cellular response to these compounds. The presence of multiple targets in the hepatocyte pathway suggests that SF-188 may be a downstream effector or a downstream product of these interactions, possibly through a metabolic or signaling cascade. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular network and the potential for multiple pathways to converge on SF-188, underscoring the importance of understanding the interplay between these compounds in cellular processes.",
